OL,3,GNEWSADriving a bus despite dyslexia
OL,4,A'changed my life'
OL,5,
OL,6,FJennifer Heaton had been looking for a
OL,7,Fjob for a year and a half and, between
OL,8,Fapplications, "didn't really do much".
OL,9,FHaving dyslexia made life difficult -
OL,10,Funtil a post on social media sent her
OL,11,Ftowards help and a new lease of life as
OL,12,Fa bus driver.
OL,14,F"It's big, it's long, it's wide, it
OL,15,Fliterally just fits on the road,"
OL,16,FHeaton says, admitting to a certain
OL,17,Famount of fear when she first took the
OL,18,Fwheel of a bus.
OL,20,FBut, after a couple of weeks, it just
OL,21,Ffelt normal, like a car, and she feels
OL,22,Fher new job has changed her life.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
